.TH KINO 1 "2026" "Kino" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kino \- play and review video
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kino
.RI [ FILE | URL "]..."
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Kino
is a video player for the Linux desktop, built on libmpv. It plays every
container and codec FFmpeg supports, decodes in hardware where the driver
allows and falls back to software where it does not, and renders subtitles
through libass.
.PP
Several arguments are opened as a playlist. Both filesystem paths and
.B http(s)
URLs are accepted.
.SH REVIEW MODE
Review mode adds SMPTE timecode, frame-exact stepping and seeking, in and out
marks, and notes attached to a specific frame. Notes are written to a sidecar
file beside the media
.RB ( <video>.kino.json )
and never modify the video. They can be exported as CSV, Markdown or PDF, and a
second reviewer's set can be imported and merged.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/kino/settings.json
Preferences. Human-readable and hand-editable on purpose.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/ch.alpinsuite.kino/
Annotation sidecars for media whose own directory is not writable.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/kino/
Seek-bar thumbnails and resume positions. Safe to delete.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_RUNTIME_DIR
Holds the per-file locks that let opening an already-playing file raise that
window instead of opening a second one. Without it, every open makes a new
window.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mpv (1)
.SH BUGS
https://github.com/AlpinSuite/kino/issues
